<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pt-BR">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<style>
    /* Configurações Gerais de Fonte e Cores */
    :root {
        --primary-color: #0f172a; /* Azul Escuro Percy */
        --accent-color: #3b82f6;  /* Azul Brilhante (Tech/Gemini) */
        --bg-color: #f8fafc;
        --card-bg: #ffffff;
        --text-color: #334155;
        --title-color: #1e293b;
    }

    body {
        font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        background-color: var(--bg-color);
        margin: 0;
        padding: 20px;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }

    /* Container Principal */
    .process-log-container {
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        position: relative;
    }

    /* Título do Log (Opcional) */
    .log-header {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: var(--primary-color);
        margin-bottom: 30px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 10px;
    }
    
    .log-header span {
        background: var(--accent-color);
        color: white;
        padding: 2px 8px;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    /* A Linha Vertical */
    .process-log-container::before {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        left: 20px; /* Posição da linha */
        width: 2px;
        background: #e2e8f0;
        z-index: 0;
    }

    /* Cada Item do Processo */
    .process-step {
        position: relative;
        margin-bottom: 25px;
        padding-left: 50px; /* Espaço para a bolinha */
        opacity: 0;
        animation: slideIn 0.5s ease-out forwards;
    }

    /* Animação em cascata para cada item */
    .process-step:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 0.1s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.2s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.3s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 0.4s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: 0.5s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(6) { animation-delay: 0.6s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(7) { animation-delay: 0.7s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(8) { animation-delay: 0.8s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(9) { animation-delay: 0.9s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(10) { animation-delay: 1.0s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(11) { animation-delay: 1.1s; }
    .process-step:nth-child(12) { animation-delay: 1.2s; }

    /* A "Bolinha" (Ícone) na Linha */
    .process-step::after {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        left: 14px; /* Ajuste fino para centralizar na linha */
        top: 5px;
        width: 14px;
        height: 14px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: white;
        border: 2px solid var(--accent-color);
        z-index: 1;
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--bg-color); /* Cria espaço visual ao redor da linha */
    }

    /* O Card de Conteúdo */
    .step-content {
        background: var(--card-bg);
        padding: 15px 20px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
        transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }

    .step-content:hover {
        transform: translateX(5px);
        border-color: var(--accent-color);
    }

    .step-title {
        margin: 0 0 8px 0;
        font-size: 1rem;
        color: var(--title-color);
        font-weight: 600;
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
    }

    .step-text {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        color: var(--text-color);
        text-align: justify;
    }

    /* Keyframes para animação */
    @keyframes slideIn {
        from {
            opacity: 0;
            transform: translateY(10px);
        }
        to {
            opacity: 1;
            transform: translateY(0);
        }
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="process-log-container">
    <div class="log-header">
        <span>AI LOG</span> Processo de Criação: Landing Page Jurídica
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Analyzing Landing Page Needs</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm currently focused on the specific requirements for Cafter Percy Advocacia's landing page. I've noted the provided logo image and will double-check for the attorney photo. My immediate priority is to understand the core message and visual style the firm wants to convey, aiming for a design that balances professionalism and approachability.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Refining Image Assumptions</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm now refining my assumptions about the provided images. While I have the logo 35 sugestão cafter percy advogado.jpg filename for the logo and will use a generated image for the lawyer, I'm second-guessing if I should use a generic placeholder instead. Since the prompt references "attachment 2," I'll assume there is a relevant image file that I just can't see, so I'll stay consistent with that assumption. The user's input suggests there is a lawyer photo, so I'll continue by using a generated lawyer photo for now.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Generating Page Elements</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm now generating initial ideas for the landing page elements. I've noted the need for a high-converting lead capture page for Cafter Percy Advocacia, targeting Labor, Social, and Social Security areas. To engage users, I'm leaning toward a multi-step form or a quiz-style approach to qualify leads, moving away from a static form. This will help build trust and support onboarding.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Developing Interaction Flow</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm now developing the interaction flow for the landing page. Building on the previous work, I've designed an interactive "Case Evaluation" tool. This tool, acting as the lead magnet, offers a more engaging experience than a static form. It has three steps and allows users to select an area (Labor, Social, or Social Security), answer a simple question, and provide contact details to receive an analysis. I will visually simulate "sending to CRM" during form submission. The design utilizes a legal theme with clean, professional visuals, with the logo and the generated lawyer photo included.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Crafting Landing Sections</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm now crafting the landing page sections. I will ensure the design is professional and emphasizes trust. I've broken the page into seven sections including the lead magnet, services, a firm bio to build trust, an FAQ, and a footer. I plan to search for relevant landing page examples and marketing trends, and I'll use the user's feedback to ensure the design meets the prompt's focus on lead generation. I will use the three main legal areas in the services section.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Refining Interaction Flow</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm currently refining the interaction flow, and I'm incorporating qualifying questions before requesting contact details to leverage the commitment principle. I'll include a visual "Analyzing..." step to simulate a personalized response, enhancing user engagement. I've confirmed image usage as planned and am researching the firm to verify its authenticity and avoid inconsistencies.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Building Engaging Questions</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm now building the engaging questions for the FAQ or quiz section. I'm focusing on crafting questions that are simple but also relevant to draw the user into the legal areas: Labor, Social, and Social Security. The objective is to make these interactions informative and engaging for the user. I'll make sure the format is concise and easy to understand to optimize the user experience.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Analyzing Law Firm Landing Pages</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I've been analyzing the content and structure of high-converting Brazilian law firm landing pages, focusing on Labor and Social Security law. I've gained insightful perspectives on effective strategies.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Designing the Onboarding Flow</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I've been working on refining the "Pre-Analysis Tool" to better capture user intent. I am now incorporating a "Rights Calculator" to better fit the need to have a smoother "onboarding" process. I am also planning on including a CRM simulation, complete with a "Protocol Number" to enhance the sense of a real system intake and improve the conversion rate.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Structuring the Landing Page</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm now focusing on the visual hierarchy and content arrangement. The logo and prominent WhatsApp button are set. The hero section with headline, subhead, and call to action is drafted. I'm building out the interactive intake tool, including the tabs, dynamic questions, and progress bar to make the process more dynamic. I'm also fleshing out the "Services Detail" cards and the "Why Us" section.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Generating Visual Assets</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm now focusing on the visual assets for the landing page. I've decided to generate a professional lawyer image with specific prompts to ensure it aligns with the Brazilian context and the law firm's brand. I'll also integrate a subtle visual cue that indicates a connection to a secure client portal within the form data process.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-content">
            <h3 class="step-title">Creating the Intake Tool</h3>
            <p class="step-text">I'm currently building the interactive intake tool, focusing on making it dynamic and intuitive. I'm prioritizing the user journey, ensuring a smooth flow through tabs, dynamic questions, and a clear progress bar. The goal is to make the process engaging, yet provide accurate data input. The inclusion of the data fields also enhances the flow.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
